.TH ZTRANSCRIBE 1 "2026-10-20" "zdots" "zdots manual"
.SH NAME
ztranscribe \- ztranscribe \-\-from\-wav <wav> \-\-output\-base <base> [options]
.SH SYNOPSIS
See OPTIONS below (generated from \fBztranscribe --help\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
Usage: ztranscribe <youtube_url> [options]
       ztranscribe --from-wav <wav> --output-base <base> [options]

High-performance YouTube transcription pipeline. Downloads best audio,
captures full metadata, and transcribes using whisper.cpp.

Options:
  --keep-media       Keep the original .wav audio file (deleted by default).
  --diarize          Identify speakers (requires HUGGINGFACE_TOKEN).
  --summarize        Generate an AI summary/cleanup (requires llama-server).
  --json-full        Emit token-level confidence (--output-json-full).
  --out-dir <dir>    Override retention dir (default ~/Downloads/transcripts).
  --prompt <text>    Bias whisper toward known vocabulary.
  --profile <p>      Whisper profile: max-accuracy (default), standard, light.
  -h, --help         Show this help

Windowed mode (Z-169, skips download):
  --prep-only        Download+convert to 16k wav, report it, stop before whisper.
  --from-wav <wav>   Transcribe a window of an existing 16k wav.
  --offset-sec <n>   Window start in seconds (with --from-wav).
  --window-sec <n>   Window length in seconds (with --from-wav).
  --output-base <b>  Whisper output-file base (required with --from-wav).

Unknown --flags are rejected (exit 1).

Outputs:
  Saved to ~/Downloads/transcripts/<video_id>/ in 5+ formats:
  .txt, .json (structured), .srt, .vtt, .csv, .info.json, .summary.md

Bot-gated sources (e.g. YouTube) need cookies. Set one of (opt-in):
  ZDOTS_YTDLP_COOKIES_FROM_BROWSER=firefox   # interactive shell only (macOS TCC restricts launchd)
  ZDOTS_YTDLP_COOKIES_FILE=/path/to/cookies.txt # Netscape format; required for background worker
  (If cookie extraction fails, yt-transcribe automatically falls back to anonymous fetch)
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
agent-guide(1), zdots-doctor(1)
